+Cluster autoscaler guidance
+
+Goal
+- Allow GPU/accelerator nodepools to scale up when workloads require additional nodes.
+
+Recommendations
+- Use cloud-native nodepool autoscaling if available (GKE node pool autoscaler, AKS VM Scale Sets, EKS Managed Node Groups).
+- Install Kubernetes Cluster Autoscaler with correct IAM permissions for EKS and appropriate flags for GKE/AKS.
+- Taint GPU nodes and use Pod tolerations to ensure non-GPU pods do not schedule on GPU nodes.
+- Tune scale-down delays to avoid thrashing for bursty inference workloads.
+
+Example for EKS:
+- Create nodegroup labeled gpu=true and enable autoscaling (ops/hw/nodepools/create_inferentia_nodepool_aws.sh as model).
+- Install cluster-autoscaler and annotate ASG to allow autoscaler to manage it.
