+# Chroma restore & DR playbook
+
+Preconditions
+- Chroma Helm deployed with persistence (PVC) and scheduled backups to S3 via CronJob.
+
+Restore steps
+1. Identify latest snapshot in S3 (e.g., s3://bucket/chroma_snapshots/YYYYMMDD.tar.gz).
+2. Copy snapshot to operator machine and extract to a temporary directory.
+3. Stop Chroma pods: kubectl scale statefulset aegis-chroma --replicas=0
+4. Replace PVC contents by restoring tarball into a new PVC or mount point (operator access required).
+5. Scale StatefulSet up and verify data present.
+6. Run application-level checks: sample queries return expected vectors and retrieval performance.
+
+Test regularly (quarterly) and record evidence manifests for DR tests.
+
